  <Patch Id="PIM04RQlDrJndWFYkHxpVT">
    <Canvas Id="E1YTsqUrSomosgDw9kyn1q" DefaultCategory="Main" BordersChecked="false" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <!--

    ************************ Application ************************

-->
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,100" Id="K51DbTFITOo2MqDXTjgIwU">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <CategoryReference Kind="Category" Name="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="KAgwYthZ2huojxWWteSu4O">
        <Canvas Id="Sd1LQJidF9lXO7Nd5UyXo0" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="VNM5oTPCIaffpa0MUWPBHG" Bounds="1300,60,480,740" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Reading a big file without freezing vvvv&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Read GeoJSON parses on the main loop, and while it parses NOTHING else in vvvv runs - not your patch, not the renderer, not the editor. Measured in vvvv 7.4, longest frame:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;      7,342 cities (this file)              0.56 s&#xD;&#xA;     56,600 roads (Natural Earth)           2.5 s&#xD;&#xA;    357,534 buildings (Delaware)            4.0 s&#xD;&#xA;  1,215,624 buildings (Connecticut)        12.9 s&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;So read in the BACKGROUND, as on the left: FileReader (String Reactive) reads the file on another thread, ForEach [Reactive] runs Read GeoJSON on that thread too, and HoldLatest hands the result to the main loop. The same node - nothing else to install. For the same four files the longest frame stayed at 0.02 - 0.04 s.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The result arrives some frames after you ask for it. LOADING is true until then, and HoldLatest keeps the previous result in the meantime.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Try it: press READ IN BACKGROUND and watch LONGEST FRAME - it stays near 0.02. Then press READ BLOCKING: it jumps to about half a second, and FRAMES stops while it parses.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Memory is the real limit: about ten times the file. Connecticut (340 MB) took vvvv to 3.8 GB. Beyond that the answer is a different format - FlatGeobuf, GeoParquet - not a cleverer GeoJSON reader.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The file carries a legacy crs member. RFC 7946 dropped it; Read GeoJSON accepts it and ignores it.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Data: Natural Earth, public domain. naturalearthdata.com">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="DZyWbq65vYkzkpCqXXj02v" Comment="File Path - 7,342 cities from Natural Earth, shipped with this package" Bounds="60,60,330,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Assets\ne_10m_populated_places_simple.geojson">
